{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/actor/2118","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"first_name","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/first_name"}],"content":"Juan","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Juan Kurchan","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"last_name","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/last_name"}],"content":"Kurchan","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"biography statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435422"}],"content":"Juan Kurchan (November 21, 1913 – November 3, 1972) was an Argentine architect, designer, and mentor of the Modern Movement in Argentina. He designed a portable seat known as the BKF Chair or butterfly chair. He was part of a group working with Le Corbusier on a plan for redevelopment of the city of Buenos Aires, and later entered the city administration and designed many new buildings there. He later became a director of the National Endowment for the Arts. (Source: Wikipedia, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Actor"}